Adaptation 06-render-and-install-consent

Added here, not in the fork. statechart and ketchup-video work in an allowed scratch folder instead of
always outside the repository and use tools that are already installed. An install runs only where the
user or the host's policy already authorized it; otherwise the user approves it immediately before it
runs. statechart renders with Pele only when it is available or its install is authorized, and
otherwise hands over the Mermaid text with the rendering limitation; its scripts/package.json drops the
test command and its test-only lockfile, because the test corpus is excluded from the collection.
babysit's round cap yields to a stricter limit in the user's or repository's instructions, and the
poteto-mode babysit playbook gains the same finite repair bound. create-formal-verification-skill
follows the same install rule; it and ketchup-video gain fallbacks for a missing statechart or ketchup.

Fork source: https://github.com/mneves75/pstack-claude commits none (this repository).
Applies to the port's plugins/pstack/skills tree after the patches numbered before it.

